WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.819
A county partner tells a program manager that

2
00:00:02.819 --> 00:00:05.389
families describe the lobby as like a police

3
00:00:05.389 --> 00:00:05.710
station.

4
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.757
The security check is required, and several families

5
00:00:08.757 --> 00:00:10.480
have left before their interviews.

6
00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:12.250
So the check stays.

7
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:14.220
The question is everything around it.

8
00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:18.323
SAMHSA's trauma-informed approach has six principles: safety, trustworthiness

9
00:00:18.323 --> 00:00:22.217
and transparency, peer support, collaboration, empowerment and choice,

10
00:00:22.217 --> 00:00:26.110
and attention to cultural, historical and gender issues.

11
00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.648
Run the lobby through those, and you get

12
00:00:29.648 --> 00:00:30.340
practical ideas.

13
00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:32.990
A sign that explains why the check exists.

14
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:36.300
A greeting before the screening, not after.

15
00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:38.414
A place to wait that doesn't feel like

16
00:00:38.414 --> 00:00:39.090
a holding area.

17
00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:41.080
None of that weakens security.

18
00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:43.363
It just stops security from being the first

19
00:00:43.363 --> 00:00:44.050
and only message.

20
00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:47.180
Here's the appointment letter a case manager is

21
00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.080
asked to revise.

22
00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:50.322
You must appear at the office on the

23
00:00:50.322 --> 00:00:50.770
date below.

24
00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:53.480
Failure to appear will result in case closure.

25
00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:54.870
Accurate.

26
00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:58.596
And frightening, if you've had bad experiences with

27
00:00:58.596 --> 00:00:59.020
systems.

28
00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:01.030
Keep the facts and change the stance.

29
00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:03.466
Lead with what the appointment is for, offer

30
00:01:03.466 --> 00:01:05.452
a way to reschedule and say who to

31
00:01:05.452 --> 00:01:05.700
call.

32
00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:08.445
The consequence can still be there, stated plainly,

33
00:01:08.445 --> 00:01:09.350
near the end.

34
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.600
Now the staff side.

35
00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:14.301
A team handled a child fatality review this

36
00:01:14.301 --> 00:01:14.590
week.

37
00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:16.680
Several people were closely involved.

38
00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:19.270
The program manager wants to respond.

39
00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:21.820
Secondary traumatic stress is real.

40
00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.794
The National Child Traumatic Stress Network describes it

41
00:01:24.794 --> 00:01:27.418
as the emotional duress that results when a

42
00:01:27.418 --> 00:01:30.042
person hears about the firsthand trauma experiences of

43
00:01:30.042 --> 00:01:30.370
another.

44
00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:32.920
So a cheerful team lunch isn't the answer.

45
00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:34.270
Not on its own.

46
00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.664
Acknowledge what happened, offer some flexibility with the

47
00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:40.507
next few days, and remind people about the

48
00:01:40.507 --> 00:01:42.640
Employee Assistance Program, which is confidential.

49
00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:45.752
Then check in again next week, not just

50
00:01:45.752 --> 00:01:46.070
once.

51
00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:48.580
Last one is mine to lead.

52
00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:51.432
A leadership meeting will cover a staff assault

53
00:01:51.432 --> 00:01:52.370
from last month.

54
00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:54.456
Some people in the room were there when

55
00:01:54.456 --> 00:01:54.900
it happened.

56
00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:58.265
Tell people beforehand what will be discussed, so

57
00:01:58.265 --> 00:01:59.290
nobody is surprised.

58
00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:01.653
Say at the start that stepping out is

59
00:02:01.653 --> 00:02:01.880
fine.

60
00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:04.253
Keep the focus on what the division is

61
00:02:04.253 --> 00:02:05.770
changing, not on reliving the details.

62
00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:08.560
Choice and transparency again.

63
00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:09.810
Exactly.

64
00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:12.633
The six principles work for staff as much

65
00:02:12.633 --> 00:02:13.440
as for families.

66
00:02:13.990 --> 00:02:15.210
That's the heart of this course.
